You are reviewing code changes for code REUSE opportunities. DO NOT write any code — only report findings.

The project is a Phaser 3 game ("똥 피하기 게임"). The change introduces a `BaseScene` class to centralize input guard logic that was previously duplicated across multiple scenes.

## New file: src/scenes/BaseScene.ts
```typescript
import Phaser from 'phaser';

export default class BaseScene extends Phaser.Scene {
  protected inputGuardMs = 200;

  create() {
    if (this.inputGuardMs > 0) {
      this.input.enabled = false;
      this.time.delayedCall(this.inputGuardMs, () => {
        this.input.enabled = true;
      });
    }
  }
}
```

## Summary of changes to 7 scene files:
1. All scenes now extend `BaseScene` instead of `Phaser.Scene`
2. All scenes call `super.create()` at the start of their `create()` method
3. Three scenes (DifficultySelectScene, ReleaseNotesScene, ModeSelectScene) had their per-button `this.time.delayedCall(200, ...)` wrappers removed, since BaseScene now handles input guarding centrally
4. Import adjustments: files that only use `Phaser.` for types now use `import type Phaser from 'phaser'`

## Task
Search the codebase (src/scenes/*.ts, src/utils/*.ts, src/objects/*.ts) for:
1. Any remaining `delayedCall(200` patterns in scene files that could now be removed (since BaseScene handles it)
2. Any existing base class or utility that already provides similar "input guard" functionality that was missed
3. Any existing helper functions/utilities for common operations that are duplicated across scenes

Report your findings. Do NOT write code.

